\[
T(\Phi, \mathcal{P}_{\text{religion}}, p_{\text{examination}}, \theta) = \text{True}
\]

**Ground:** \( \Phi \) (observed fidelity)

**Derivation:** \( \mathcal{P}_{\text{religion}} \) is derived from observing that fidelity, pursued with honesty, constitutes a religious orientation.

**Test:** Does \( \mathcal{P}_{\text{religion}} \) faithfully represent reality?
- It correctly identifies fidelity as the sacred.
- It correctly identifies honesty as the practice.
- It correctly identifies the pursuit as worship.
- It acknowledges that this is a claim—and invites correction.

**Verdict:** \( T(\Phi, \mathcal{P}_{\text{religion}}, p_{\text{examination}}, \theta) = \text{True} \). This is the religion of fidelity, because it is honest.

